@host = http://localhost:5000

### Step 2: baseline, always hits the database (~500 ms)
GET {{host}}/products/1/no-cache

### Step 2: cache-aside (1st call: database, next calls: cache)
GET {{host}}/products/1

### Step 2: product that doesn't exist (always hits the database: cache penetration)
GET {{host}}/products/999

### Step 3: warm the cache without jitter (all keys expire together)
POST {{host}}/cache/warm

### Step 3: warm the cache with jitter (expirations spread out)
POST {{host}}/cache/warm?jitter=true

### Database queries and cache hits/misses/errors
GET {{host}}/stats

### Reset counters
POST {{host}}/stats/reset

### Cache health (stays 200 with status "degraded" when Valkey is down)
GET {{host}}/health

### Dashboard: open http://localhost:5000 in a browser (Development only)

### Valkey INFO + DBSIZE (Development only)
GET {{host}}/valkey/info

### Keys matching a pattern, with TTL (Development only)
GET {{host}}/valkey/keys?pattern=product:*

### One key: type, TTL and value (Development only)
GET {{host}}/valkey/key?key=product:1

### Delete a key: manual invalidation (Development only)
DELETE {{host}}/valkey/key?key=product:1

### Burst: 200 simultaneous lookups over 5 ids (Development only)
POST {{host}}/lab/burst?requests=200&distinctIds=5

### FLUSHDB (Development only)
POST {{host}}/valkey/flush
